WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.702
-Thanks, everyone.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:05.772
I -- I...I spend...

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:10.376
what I would call an inordinate
amount of time on the Internet,

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:11.911
doing really
stupid things.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.013
Doing things that I'm n--
like replying to e-mails

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:16.583
that are not necessarily
meant for me.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.817
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:21.687
I -- I have, uh --
I have veitch@domain.com

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:23.022
for my e-mail address.
And what that means is that,

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:24.757
if someone misses off
the initial,

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.592
I get the e-mail.
So, I get a lot of e-mails

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.562
for Veitchs who,
I have no idea who they are.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:30.663
I got an e-mail
that was addressed

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.831
to Alan and Deb Veitch.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.166
I have literally no idea
who these people are.

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:36.469
But it said "Please review
the cash estimate."

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:37.837
And it was from a --
It was a company --

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:38.838
It was a
swimming-pool company.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.140
A guy called,
basically, Lex...

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.410
runs a company called
Relex Pools.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.012
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.220
And the pool was
102 LF, right?

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.489
And I thought -- I thought I'd
test the water, so to speak...

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.190
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.092
...and I said,
"Look, what does LF, uh --

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:01.828
What does LF
stand for?"

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.597
And...

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.499
they got back in touch.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.968
And they said, "LF stands
for 'linear feet.'"

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.203
Janice...

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.938
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.938 --> 00:01:14.874
...did not seem
to mind or notice

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.843
the fact that I was neither
Alan nor Deb.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.745
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.549
I thought,
"That's interesting."

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:25.017
She said,
"See attached plans."

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:26.352
Now, she attached these plans
of the proposed swimming pool.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.586
So, basically, you guys,
you've got, here --

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:28.721
You've got the, uh...

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.990
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:36.830
We've got the neighboring
houses, some foliage,

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.931
and up at the top left
we've got this --

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:40.867
Alan and Deb's house.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:41.934
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.870
And then,
that's the proposed pool.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.738
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.173
And I want to be
very clear about this, guys --

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.909
you should never reply to an
e-mail that's not meant for you.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.844
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.379
You shouldn't do it.
-Why?

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.947
-Because you should just
delete the e-mail,

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:56.983
let the people know
they've made a terrible mistake.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.654
However...

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.157
looking at that...

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:08.294
I don't know about you,
but to me...

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.530
I just didn't think Alan and Deb
were gonna be happy with that.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.900
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.935
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.441
I said "Janice,
I'm gonna be frank..."

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.643
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.781
"...I'm unhappy with
the size of the pool."

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.483
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:37.290
"Mr. Veitch, it's not legal
to build on private property.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.192
The pool is as large
as it can be

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:43.262
without encroaching on
your neighbor's property."

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:45.598
I said,
"Old Man McPhearson?"

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.900
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.936
"He won't mind."

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:54.774
I said, "We're still skimping
on the size of the pool.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:58.677
I don't want people
to come around and be like,

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.079
'Where's the pool?'"

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:02.248
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.450
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.789
"Balls on the line,
Janice."

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:11.824
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:18.263
"It needs to be larger."

00:03:18.263 --> 00:03:19.866
She said,
"How much larger?"

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:23.269
I said, "Boom."

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.771
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:28.141
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.483
"That is not possible."

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.152
No [bleep], Janice.

00:03:41.453 --> 00:03:44.857
"We cannot build
that close to the property."

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.159
"Well, if the property
is a problem,

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.695
I'll take out
the property."

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.396
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:56.102
I'll be honest --
I thought, based upon that,

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.938
that she would know
that I was joking.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.773
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:04.142 --> 00:04:06.112
"Where will you live?"

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:07.947
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.650
[ Applause ]

00:04:13.585 --> 00:04:14.854
I said, "Boom."

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:17.790
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.993
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:25.831 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:27.867
-James Veitch.

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:31.404
Look out for his comedy special
later this year.

